From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:20:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmgr-pwrstate: Keep sleep-retained domains
 on in system sleep

The J713's G16 GPU has no system-sleep callbacks, so in the noirq
phase genpd powers its GFX domain off, and the TVM gate above it, under
the running GPU firmware; the power-on at resume then times out. Let a
domain marked apple,sleep-retained decline its power-off while the
system sleeps: genpd then keeps it and its parents on. Runtime power
management is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 8fd377b7d93eea9d1951c9c915c827c5ad80cc30)
[dylan: this tree has no apple,inherited-on; only the sleep_retained
 field, its read and the power_off check apply. system_sleep is set from
 suspend_late to resume_early here, as in the original.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
index 808f45a2b6..942c994030 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
@@ -50,6 +50,8 @@ struct apple_pmgr_ps {
 	bool externally_clocked;
 	bool system_sleep;
 	bool firmware_owned;
+	/* apple,sleep-retained: kept on while the system sleeps */
+	bool sleep_retained;
 	/* Never enable automatic power management (apple,no-auto-pm). */
 	bool no_auto_pm;
 };
@@ -183,6 +185,9 @@ static int apple_pmgr_ps_power_off(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd)
 
 	if (ps->firmware_owned)
 		return 0;
+	/* A live coprocessor keeps this domain through system sleep. */
+	if (ps->sleep_retained && ps->system_sleep)
+		return -EBUSY;
 
 	ret = apple_pmgr_ps_set(genpd, APPLE_PMGR_PS_PWRGATE, false);
 	if (ret)
@@ -348,6 +353,7 @@ static int apple_pmgr_ps_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * it, keep it on and never change its target or automatic gating.
 	 */
 	ps->firmware_owned = of_property_read_bool(node, "apple,firmware-owned");
+	ps->sleep_retained = of_property_read_bool(node, "apple,sleep-retained");
 
 	ret = of_property_read_u32(node, "apple,min-state", &ps->min_state);
 	if (ret == 0 && ps->min_state <= APPLE_PMGR_PS_ACTIVE && !ps->firmware_owned)
